      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T22:34:08Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion,app): tighten the axis fit's inlier band to the revolve's own noise\n\nThe robust axis fit sorted normal lines with the 3 % sagitta band\n(0.3 mm on an r10 bar), so facets standing near a meridian plane\nwithout lying in one - a cross hole's mouth ring, its floor's centre\nstrip - stayed inliers and leaned the line ~0.001 mm, past the lathe\nspindle law's 0.0005 mm: a bar with one modelled cross hole was refused.\n\nOnce the inliers settle, the band now shrinks to 4x the kept facets'\narea-weighted median miss (floor 1e-9 of the radius) and the line is\nrefitted, repeated while the band keeps shrinking. Every tightened\nrefit must pass the same backstops and the full judgement on all\nfacets; one that fails is not taken and the last settled (trusted) fit\nstands. An exact revolve meets the tight band everywhere and keeps its\nplain fit bit for bit. The spindle law's 0.0005 is unchanged.\n\nPins: lathe_cross_drill a_bar_with_one_modelled_cross_hole_fits_on_\nthe_spindle_and_drills_clean (main reads worst 0.00088 mm, refused),\naxis_robust a_near_meridian_strip_is_set_aside_by_the_tightened_band\n(main 3.3e-4 mm off), a_rectangular_prism_is_still_refused_as_not_\nrevolved. The punched_bar fixture's half-turn mirror holes (#117\nworkaround) are dropped; the cross-drill suites stay green without them.\n\nFixes #116\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
