        "date": "2026-11-07T22:59:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): tighten the axis fit once, from a noise scale, and only on improvement\n\nReview of PR #168. The iterated median-shrink band picked facets by the\nsign of their noise on noisy meshes and settled on axes worse than the\nplain fit, still trusted; and the set-aside share, read at the tight\nband, named noise as features on plain bars.\n\n- The wide band is now max(3 % radius, 5 sigma), sigma the MAD scale of\n  every facet's miss about the plain fit: a band inside the noise cut\n  its tails one-sidedly (main did this past ~15 um of jitter too).\n- The wide trim is taken only when it lowers the clipped residual of\n  every facet.\n- The tightening runs ONCE: band 5 sigma of the coarse inliers, one\n  refit with no re-trim, taken only when it passes every gate and lowers\n  the coarse inliers' clipped residual. Declined, the wide fit stands\n  trusted.\n- outlier_share is read at the wide band.\n- Tests move to axis_robust_tests.rs (400-line law).\n\nPins: a_noisy_shaft_with_a_strip_never_fits_worse_than_plain (32-case\njitter x strip sweep, 0.2-17 um; 1 um + strip: 1.8e-4 vs plain 7.0e-4),\na_noisy_plain_shaft_sets_nothing_aside (jitter 1e-5..1e-2 and an f32\nshaft at X1234.5 report 0 set aside).\n\nRefs #116\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
